//g.nexonstatic.com/media/dmihv2bh/water-cannon-v2.png Water Cannon
Damage has been increased for all Ranks.For Dan 3:Before: 152 ~ 175After: 228 ~ 262When fully charging Water Cannon (5 charges), a splash range of 2m will now be applied.Depending on the number of charges, different Stardust skills will activate.1 ~ 4 Charges: Blast5 Charges: FlareThe delay upon using the skill has been reduced.An upper limit has been applied for casting speed (up to 35%).
//g.nexonstatic.com/media/lj3fbl3g/flame-burst-v2.png Flame Burst
Damage has been increased for all Ranks.For Dan 3:Before: 24 ~ 46After: 48 ~ 92
//g.nexonstatic.com/media/piuhbdbu/life-drain.png Life Drain
The HP/sec recovery has been increased at all levels.For Rank 1:Before: 300 HP/secAfter: 450 HP/sec
//g.nexonstatic.com/media/cinffjtf/heat-buster.png Heat Buster
Damage has been increased for all Ranks.For Rank 1:Before: 695 ~ 1175After: 1390 ~ 2350Splash Damage is now applied 100% of the time.The skill’s range has been increased from 7m to 15m.You will no longer fall backwards when the skill triggers a Critical Hit.The distance your character is pushed back upon use of the skill has been shortened.The delay upon using the skill has been reduced.Pressure build-up when using Alchemy Skills has been reduced, excluding Flame Burst.The “Immediately Activate Skill on Target” option now applies to Heat Buster.Some changes have been made to the Alchemy Mastery Bonus formula calculation.When using the skill with Elemental Wave and Time Shift, pressure build-up will only reach 75% instead of 100%.
//g.nexonstatic.com/media/msodmcom/elemental-wave.png Elemental Wave
The skill’s effect will no longer be a single-charge and instead last for 60 seconds.When using Life Drain while under Elemental Wave’s effect, the additional health recovery has been increased.For Rank 1: 10% → 200%.
//g.nexonstatic.com/media/oxpfa12h/alchemy-mastery.png Miscellaneous Changes:
The crystal storage for the Revenant Insight Guard Cylinder and Perseus Tyrannus Guard Cylinder has been increased from 1,000 to 5,000.Damage Coefficients from HP, MP, and Stamina have been improved.Puppetry
//g.nexonstatic.com/media/e0vehy31/control-marionette.png Control Marionette
The puppet will now receive 100% of the Puppeteer’s Damage, Critical, Balance, Defense Penetration, and Piercing Level.The minimum control distance for marionettes have been increased from 3m to 10m.The maximum controllable distance for marionettes have been increased from 13m to 20m.The cooldown when disconnecting from your marionette has been reduced from 1 second to 0.5 seconds.When disconnected from your marionette, a circle will now appear around the marionette to display the distance needed to regain control of a marionette.Marionettes are now immune to standard knockback and freeze.
//g.nexonstatic.com/media/snupzii2/act-1.png Act 1: Inciting Incident
Damage has increased at all ranks.For Rank 1:Before: 320%After: 480%The range of the attack has been increased from 8.5m to 15m for all ranks.Distance will now be measured based on the position on the character.
 //g.nexonstatic.com/media/1fcbi4wj/act-2.png Act 2: Threshold Cutter
Damage has increased at all ranks.For Rank 1:Before: 960% (280% + 280% + 400%)After: 1344% (392% + 392% + 560%)The knockback distance on a target has been reduced.
 //g.nexonstatic.com/media/qleljc32/act-4.png Act 4: Rising Action
Damage has increased at all ranks.For Dan 3:Before: 680%After: 1020%The knockback distance on a target has been reduced.When the skill is loaded, an attack range circle will now appear.
//g.nexonstatic.com/media/gzvbvwlu/act-6.png Act 6: Crisis
The Pull effect of the skill has been improved to occur regardless of the monster's knockback gauge.
//g.nexonstatic.com/media/5aulpync/act-7.png Act 7: Climactic Crash
Damage has been increased and modified at all ranks to allow for major damage on the first hit, with additional smaller damage on subsequent hits.For Rank 1:Before: 860%After: 2580% (Initial Hit) + 100% (Subsequent Hits)Enemies in the path of the skill will now be pushed towards the attack’s direction rather than to the side.Marionettes now charge at a faster speed during the skill.The length of the attack range has been increased from 4m to 5m.The knockback distance on enemies has been increased from 4m to 5m.A cooldown penalty will no longer occur when cancelling the skill.Simplenogi: Part 2
Simplenogi: Part 2 Update has arrived! 🎉
Item tooltips have been improved, and the way text displayed has changed.When applying simplified mode, you can see only the key information such as level or effect name in an abbreviated form.When applying detailed mode, you can see more detailed information than before.Similar information has been colour coded for quick and easy viewing.Added list icons and indentation to make information more recognizable.You can switch between simplified mode and detailed mode by pressing the ALT key while the equipment item tooltip is displayed.Item tooltips are no longer obscured by announcements.The item selection window has been improved.Changed to a vertical scroll type that can expand up and down.Modified to a 2-column list format.Item search and sorting functions are added.
