Debuff Changes
//g.nexonstatic.com/media/rijlnqnu/pragarah.png Brionac and Seal: Pragarah
The shredding effects of Brionac and Seal: Pragarah have been unified:Awakened Brionac (by use of Awakening of Light or Shock) will now also reduce Magic Defense and Magic Protection on hit, according to the level of your Seal: Pragarah technique.Seal: Pragarah, when activated, will now also reduce Protection.The shredding effects of Brionac and Seal: Pragarah have been strengthened:Protection:Before: 3 per hitAfter: 6 per hitMagic Defense and Magic ProtectionBefore: 3 at technique level 10After: 6 at technique level 10Status Effect icons have been added to the enemy to indicate when they are at maximum Protection shred, or maximum Magic Defense/Magic Protection shred, from these sources.//g.nexonstatic.com/media/ncmindce/physical-debuff.png //g.nexonstatic.com/media/tzbjuwc5/magical-debuff.png[table][tr][td]【 Developer Comments 】
Use of Brionac and Seal: Pragarah to reduce enemy Defense/Protection/Magic Defense/Magic Protection is an important part of Mabinogi combat. We felt that the process to use both sources to apply the two effects separately was an uncomfortable play pattern. In order to make this smoother, we have unified the effects of Brionac and Seal: Pragarah so that instead players pick which application source to use depending on the situation. Additionally, we increased the shred per hit so that less hits are required to reach the cap, and added a status effect icon so you can quickly check if the enemy has reached the cap or not.[/td][/tr][tr][td]【 Mabinogi Team Note 】
Additionally, we intend to rename Pragarah and Seal: Pragarah in a future update to Fragarach and Seal: Fragarach. This change is intended to correct the name of this mythological weapon. While we sympathize that changing terms players have become accustomed to can have challenges, we do want to represent the source material in an accurate, educational, and entertaining manner.
- The Mabinogi Team[/td][/tr][/table]
//g.nexonstatic.com/media/lrxhearc/hydra-transformation.png Hydra Transmutation
The Battle Alchemy talent skill Hydra Transmutation has been adjusted.
An indicator has been added to display the attack range of your Hydra.The time the Magic Defense and Magic Protection reduction is applied has been increased.30 seconds at Rank 1[table][tr][td]
【 Developer Comments 】
Hydra Transmutation is a considerable skill for Magic Attack based talents. However, due to the fixed location of the Hydra, it can be difficult to apply the Magic Defense / Magic Protection shred. We have decided to improve the skill to allow for more effective application of this debuff by making it last for a longer duration after an enemy enters its area of effect.[/td][/tr][/table]
Pet Friend Summon Improvements
Pet Parade, a new action, has been added.//g.nexonstatic.com/media/o15ahmhy/pet-parade.pngThis action can be learned by adding an extra Friend Summon slot to a pet by using Fynn Sync, or by summoning a pet that has an extra Friend Summon slot already unlocked.When used with a summoned pet with Friend Summon slots set, Pet Parade will activate the pet’s 1~5 Friend Summon slots that are ready to be summoned in sequential order.Friend Summons can still be individually summoned like before.Friend Summon slots can now be updated once every five minutes per slot, changed from once every Erinn day.Increased the duration of the Magic Defense and Magic Protection shreds provided by the summon skill for Ceraunus-type pets, Lightning Wave.Before: 30 secondsAfter: 5 minutes
Boss Health Bars
//g.nexonstatic.com/media/suufnqvm/boss-health-bar.png
The duration for debuffs will now show on the health bars for certain bosses. The list is as follows:Succubus QueenSkelemancerIllusion of BalorCethlennFleurKeruneMag Mell Guard​ CaptainMag Mell Magic SpiritSrengIrusanCompleted Glas GhaibhleannGiga Glas GhaibhleannCailleachUnfinished ReverieCnoc OighirThe Winter TyrantDebuffs with a timer will display the remaining time directly below the icon.
Other Debuff Changes

The following debuffs have had Status Effect icons added:
Combo: Spinning Uppercut //g.nexonstatic.com/media/sd4nkxpm/spinning-uppercut-debuff.pngSmokescreen //g.nexonstatic.com/media/cblbctob/smokescreen-debuff.pngDeath Mark //g.nexonstatic.com/media/v0jlv1xy/death-mark-debuff.pngWater Balloon //g.nexonstatic.com/media/npnjk4lm/water-balloon-debuff.pngPatch Notes
Fantasy Life Changes
We have updated our Recommended Hardware Specifications from Windows 7 to Windows 10.Adjusted the following search fields to no longer be Case SensitiveInventory SearchNPC ShopDressing RoomFace Accessory slot renamed to Facewear.All item names that previously stated (Face Accessory Slot Only) have been shortened to (Facewear).The Dressing Room category has been renamed.Blaanid and Growth Guide have been updated to improve the flow for new players.The Header text for these quests has been changed to [Guide].The messages seen when attempting to open the Memoir Book or Growth Guide before unlocking have been updated to better indicate how to unlock them.A step has been added to the unlock quests to require you to open the respective UI once.Once per day, resetting at 7am (Server Time), you may speak with Blaanid to restore a missing Blossoming Memories weapon, if far enough in the questline.Adjustments have been made to several Storyline Missions to improve places where players may get stuck.
G7 - Ruwai’s Exploration Journal has been improved to allow players to progress quicker, and immediately teleport to the ruins entrance by speaking with Ruwai.During G7 - Lost Memory of the Ancients, Kousai's Lipai Tea can be reacquired by speaking with Kousai if the original tea is lost.The descriptions in the 'List of Missing People' during G22 - Overlapping Trails has been improved.The objective text to find Ruairi during G8 - Legatus' Advice has been made more clear.The required Synthesis materials will be regranted if necessary upon entering G10 - Goddess Memorial mission.During G17 - Mysterious Clue, completing the first objective will regrant the Mysterious Lingerie if the item is not in your inventory.During G3 - Deliver the Spirit Potion, the Spirit Potion can be regranted by speaking with Duncan if the item is lost.Fixed an issue where you could not enter the Barri Dungeon with a Brown Fomor Pass in the G1 - Paradise quest if you had a Fomor Medal.The quest description for several quests has been updated to indicate that you can reobtain the necessary quest item by speaking with a certain NPC.Auto-pathing has been improved further.The option to move to a specific NPC via the NPC Search or by Quest has been added.The Chronicle Mission, The First Battle of Mag Tuireadh, has been updated.The experience for clearing the mission has been increased.When picking your role as The One in the Spotlight, fewer cutscenes will show to increase the speed of repeat performances.The effects of the Sealed Letters hidden within the battlefield have been strengthened.A light ray has been added to Sealed Letters that have been found on previous runs, making it easier to find in subsequent performances.The guide quest, Encore for an Empty Theater, has been improved.The cost to craft a Chronicle Celtic Weapon has been reduced from 5 Celtic Artifact Shards to 3 Celtic Artifact Shards.Several enemies have been adjusted to be easier.Improvements to emptying bags have been made. The items from the emptied bag will automatically be organized into the free space of other bags.The items will be sorted based on bag order and bag tag settings.Items will no longer be moved into the Temporary Inventory or drop onto the floor.If you do not have enough free space, you will not be able to empty the bag.
Bug Fixes
Quite a few smaller fixes this update, thank you all for your finds and patience when issues do arise. The usual text polish has continued this month, this time a few fixes for G24 and G25, miscellaneous quests, the descriptions for Mysterious Spirit Stones, and realigning a few UI text boxes.After the March Title menu update, custom Guild titles on your title list were defaulting to "an Erinn Expeditionary Force Member". This has been fixed to once again show as your custom guild title on this UI.An issue occurred when Constellation Casting caused constellations to be placed only on the right side, and occasionally hiding stars beneath the UI. The stars were brightest overhead with the launch of Astrologer, but now it's time for star fishers to truly test their mettle.Outfit Motions that contained additional props (such as a cat, or a kettle) would flicker upon starting your running animation. This has been corrected.The display issue causing ducats to appear incorrectly when at values over 4.3 billion has been fixed. To those who sallied forth to attempt to replicate this issue before it was fixed- we hope you all made your goal in time!The Auction House entries for expiring Tail coupons have been removed to clean up items that cannot be obtained.A rarely occurring dark umbral shroud causing reduced vision and spooky vibes upon renewed entry into one of the many dungeons of Uladh has been dispelled.
Bugs fixed during the 3/20 Maintenance
An issue was fixed where the Warm and Conceited Maid Partner Shops would appear as empty. Some say this was the impact of the Clumsy Maid, but surely none would hear such slander.Glewyas, tired from politely correcting nobles in the proper way to say his name, was accidentally taking Gold in lieu of Food Court Seals. He has been ordered to get a good night's rest.Pan is still learning the ropes after taking over the Check-In Attendance from Irusan. He made a small mistake with the date on the stamps, causing them to appear as if he had done this months in the past! He's fixed his mistakes, and hopes you wool forgive him.
Known Bugs
https://nxcache.nexon.net/cms/2024/q2/1592/bug_catching.pngDoll Bag Storage Chests are currently missing its "Doll Info" on its Item Attributes Section.The Brionac and Seal: Pragarah are currently operating at half-power by not reducing an enemy's Magic Defense and Magic Protection.There are currently issues causing the Blacklist to not work as expected for some players.Under periodic conditions, Milletians will be temporarily unable to duel other Milletians.There is an issue with the in-game Guild list not populating with guilds.
